{%- comment -%}
  Newsletter form. Shared by the popup, the footer and the newsletter
  section. snippet_context tells them apart: 'popup', 'footer', 'section'.

  CAPTURE SPLIT, 15 Sep 2026. The three routes used to emit one identical
  tag string, so the joining-gift audience and the news audience were the
  same audience as far as Shopify was concerned. They now tag differently:

    popup   -> prospect,gift,popup     the joining gift
    footer  -> prospect,news,footer    news and broadcasts only
    section -> prospect,news,section   news and broadcasts only, the Join page

  The else branch defaults to news, not gift, on purpose. A miswired form
  that hands out a newsletter is cheaper than one that hands out money.

  Shopify customer tags ride across into Klaviyo as a profile property.
  The Klaviyo segments read that tag, and the flows trigger off the segments.

  SUCCESS STATE. Popup only. Footer and section keep the theme default,
  because a full success panel in a footer would be absurd.

  THE EMAIL PROMISE IS GONE, 15 Sep 2026. This panel used to say the code
  was on its way, which was false on a live storefront because the Klaviyo
  welcome flow has never sent. The code is now printed on screen, so the
  panel delivers the thing itself and promises nothing. Once the welcome
  flow is live and proven by a real test signup, a line about the email
  can be added back. Not before.

  THE EMAIL PROMISE IS BACK, 13 Oct 2026. Operator ruling. The welcome
  flow is live and sends each first-time signup a one-time £10 code, so the
  panel says the code is on its way and no longer prints WELCOME. The line
  opens with "First order with us?" because the gift now works on a first
  order only. The welcome segment in Klaviyo needs no placed order, and both
  Shopify discounts are limited to customers who have not purchased. A past
  buyer who signs up gets no code email, and the opening question keeps the
  panel true for them. WELCOME itself stays valid to 31 January 2027 for
  anyone who saw it on screen before this change.

  THE GIFT IS NOW DESCRIBED AS TEN POUNDS PLUS FREE DELIVERY, 15 Sep 2026.
  Operator ruling. It is true on every case: the cheapest case still clears
  the free delivery threshold after the ten pounds comes off, so delivery
  is free on any case the gift can be used on. The geography stays in the
  line because delivery is not free everywhere. If a case is ever priced
  low enough that the gift drops it under the threshold, this line becomes
  false and must be changed back.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  case snippet_context
    when 'popup'
      assign capture_tags = 'prospect,gift,popup'
    when 'footer'
      assign capture_tags = 'prospect,news,footer'
    else
      assign capture_tags = 'prospect,news,section'
  endcase
-%}

{%- assign nl_placeholder = 'general.newsletter_form.newsletter_email' | t -%}
{%- assign nl_submit = 'general.newsletter_form.submit' | t -%}
{%- if placeholder_text != blank -%}{%- assign nl_placeholder = placeholder_text -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- if submit_text != blank -%}{%- assign nl_submit = submit_text -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- assign newsletter_form_id = 'newsletter-' | append: section_id -%}
{% form 'customer', id: newsletter_form_id %}
  {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}
    {%- if snippet_context == 'popup' -%}
      <div class="tl-joined">
        <p class="tl-joined__head">You're in.</p>
        <p class="tl-joined__body">First order with us? Your £10 code is on its way to your inbox.</p>
        <a href="/collections/cases" class="btn tl-joined__btn">Start with a case</a>
        <p class="tl-joined__fine">£10 off your first case, delivered free to England, Scotland and Wales. Cases only, one per customer.</p>
      </div>
    {%- else -%}
      <div class="note note--success">
        {{ 'general.newsletter_form.newsletter_confirmation' | t }}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if form.errors and form.context == snippet_context -%}
    {{ form.errors | default_errors }}
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- unless form.posted_successfully? -%}
    <label for="Email-{{ section_id }}" class="hidden-label">{{ 'general.newsletter_form.newsletter_email' | t }}</label>
    <label for="newsletter-form-submit-{{ section_id }}" class="hidden-label">{{ 'general.newsletter_form.submit' | t }}</label>
    <input type="hidden" name="contact[tags]" value="{{ capture_tags }}">
    <input type="hidden" name="contact[context]" value="{{ snippet_context }}">
    <div class="input-group newsletter__input-group">
      <input type="email" value="{% if customer %}{{ customer.email }}{% endif %}" placeholder="{{ nl_placeholder }}" name="contact[email]" id="Email-{{ section_id }}" class="input-group-field newsletter__input" autocorrect="off" autocapitalize="off" required>
      <div class="input-group-btn">
        <button type="submit" id="newsletter-form-submit-{{ section_id }}" class="btn" name="commit">
          <span class="form__submit--large">{{ nl_submit }}</span>
          <span class="form__submit--small">
            {%- if submit_text != blank -%}
              {{ nl_submit }}
            {%- else -%}
              <svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" role="presentation" class="icon icon--wide icon-arrow-right" viewBox="0 0 50 15"><title>icon-right-arrow</title><path d="M0 9.63V5.38h35V0l15 7.5L35 15V9.63Z"/></svg>
            {%- endif -%}
          </span>
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  {%- endunless -%}
{% endform %}

<style>
  .tl-joined{text-align:center;padding:4px 0 2px}
  .tl-joined__head{margin:0 0 8px;font-size:22px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:600}
  .tl-joined__body{margin:0 0 18px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5}
  .tl-joined__btn{display:inline-block;width:100%}
  .tl-joined__fine{margin:12px 0 0;font-size:12px;line-height:1.4;opacity:.7}
</style>
